en:
Heh heh...
The story I'm about to tell you is that kind of story.
A story about fate.{p}

Perhaps a god by the name of devil dwelt in that Rubelize too.
Or perhaps something unknowable had taken possession of the organ.
The day finally came when her wish was granted.{p}

And in her hospital bed, she dreamed of that future and waited for the day she'd be discharged.
But a zaibatsu heiress dreaming such a modest dream? If you ask me, that's a luxurious kind of selfishness.
Ordinary people can hardly make even such modest dreams come true.{p}

From her father's point of view, that organ was the very thing that had destroyed his daughter's dreams and hopes.
Even if it was just an organ with no will of its own, he couldn't let it be.
But she hated her father for it.{p}

...Heh heh.
Yes, unless it happened to you yourself, you couldn't believe a fairy tale like this, could you?
...Well then, I'll go on with Okawa's story.{p}

Heh heh...
Anyone might think so.
No, isn't it less that she couldn't be happy, and more that you just don't want someone like that to be happy, {a}{f:|}?{p}

...Let's get back to Okawa, shall we?
The doorbell at Okawa's house kept ringing, again and again.
Because she didn't come to the door right away.{p}

That's the end of my story.
...Still, the seventh one is awfully late.
Now then, what shall we do...?{p}

...Let's get back to Okawa, shall we?
"Excuse me! Delivery!"
She heard a young man's voice from the other side of the door.{p}

But the ghost's strength was too great, and she couldn't resist.
Okazaki's ghost showed no mercy.
She strangled Okawa, stuffed her mouth full, and left her unable to breathe.{p}

"Gh... aughh..."
Okawa let out a low groan and collapsed.
And then, just like that, she breathed her last...{p}

Heh heh...
Hopeless Okawa.
She had drive enough to dig up a grave, so why didn't she try to walk the road of her fate on her own strength?{p}

The day Okazaki stayed late at school was during exam period.
She was studying in the library.
During exams there were no club activities, and many people went straight home, so the school was quieter than usual.{p}

She left the library and walked down the hallway.
She thought it was about time she went home.
And as she was passing the music room...{p}

Okazaki apologized to the girl and turned to leave.
She looked away from the music room and stepped off down the hallway.
And after she'd taken a few steps...{p}

After that, Okazaki went back to the music room after school time and time again.
But she never saw that girl again.
It was around then that Okazaki received the Rubelize from her father.{p}

She clutched the Rubelize and prayed.
She wanted to know who the woman playing the organ in the music room really was.
And then she headed for the music room again.{p}

(M... Mother!☆)
In her heart, Okazaki called out to the clear-voiced woman.
And then...{p}

A woman's low voice spoke, and Okazaki felt a blow to her head.
A shock, as if someone had struck her.
And then she lost consciousness...{p}

"You shouldn't be messing around with that organ...
It doesn't make a sound anymore.
It's broken, you see..."{p}

Okazaki was startled.
And this is what she thought.
...She would find out who the woman playing the organ really was.{p}

(Mother☆)
She desperately called out to the woman with the low voice.
And then...{p}

"Yukie... I am not your mother.
I never said a single word of the sort, did I?"
That was the reply that came back.{p}

(Oh no☆)
That was what Okazaki felt in that instant.
She had a feeling the woman with the low voice was going to curse her to death, then and there.{p}

Iwashita was watching {f:me|me}, smiling.
{f:I|I} prayed silently.
Please, let me become {f:rich|rich}...!{p}

Iwashita's smile warped.
I couldn't stay on my feet anymore.{p}As I collapsed to the floor, {f:I|I} realized my wish had come true, and I was going to be rich.
Yes... from my family's insurance money, which I would be receiving soon.{p}

Heh heh...
Do you really think so?
If you do, you're far too naive.{p}

Iwashita was watching {f:me|me}, smiling.
{f:I|I} prayed silently.
Please, let me become a genius...!{p}

Something went thump inside my head.
I could feel my blood vessels throbbing.
Somehow it was hard to breathe.{p}
